        "original_id": "088b12f1-6dc4-50e2-9497-a7e02c7f948f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Concepts: Orgasmic platform, Sensate focusing\n- People: William H. Masters, Virginia E. Johnson\n- Organizations: Masters and Johnson research team\n- Topics: Human sexual response, Sexual disorders and dysfunctions\n\nFacts:\n- From 1957 until the 1990s, the Masters and Johnson research team pioneered research into the nature of human sexual response and the diagnosis and treatment of sexual disorders and dysfunctions.\n- The Masters and Johnson research team was composed of William H. Masters and Virginia E. Johnson.\n- Masters and Johnson introduced the term sensate focusing.\n- Sensate focusing was aimed at increasing personal and interpersonal awareness of self and the other's needs.\n- Masters and Johnson labeled the orgasmic platform as the tissues of the outer third of the vagina.",
